  "facts": [
    "The Mont Blanc Tunnel, opened 19 July 1965, stretches 11.611 km beneath the Alps, lying 2,480 m below the Aiguille du Midi—making it the world’s second deepest operational highway tunnel.",
    "Construction began in 1959, requiring 711 t tonnes of explosives to blast 555,000 m³ of rock, and 4.6 million man‑hours from five engineers and 350 workers.",
    "After a deadly 1999 fire that killed 39 people, the tunnel was closed until 2002 and now operates under a single 50‑50 joint company, MBT‑EEIG, ensuring unified safety management."
